    ["　　这一年的最后一天，森林遭遇了百年未遇的暴雪，猫头鹰长老召集起了一场紧急会议。\n\n　　 “北边山洞上方的积雪发生了崩塌，那里面还住着冬眠的蝙蝠一家，我们不能放着它们不管。”\n\n　　所有的动物都沉默了，它们基本不和蝙蝠来往，只有邓恩在去年春天去过那个洞穴，但它早就忘记里面什么样了。\n\n　　“我们去吧！”戴莉跳到了鹿角顶端，“就算你在里面迷失了方向，我的歌声也能把我们带到正确的道路上。”\n\n　　它们就这样进入了洞穴，里面结构错综复杂，邓恩和戴莉费了不少力气才找到受伤的蝙蝠一家。就在它们准备离开洞穴的时候，外面狂风大作，无数雪花被风裹挟而来，挡住了所有的光。邓恩又尝试了几个方向，比找不到出口更令人绝望的是蝙蝠一家越来越微弱的呼吸。\n\n　　戴莉飞到了它耳边开始歌唱，金色的旋律指引抚平了邓恩有些焦躁的心情，他沿着音符亮起的方向走去。十米，五十米，一百米……眼前仍然没有出现洞口的光亮，戴莉意识到前往出口的代价可能比想象中更多。\n\n　　没有犹豫。\n\n　　它飞得更高了，飞到邓恩根本看不清的地方，歌唱到背上的羽毛所剩无几，她开始下坠。\n\n　　眼前还是没有出现光亮。"] = "On the last day of the year, the forest encountered a blizzard unseen in a century, and the Owl Elder called an emergency meeting. \n\n \"The snow above the northern cave has collapsed, and a family of hibernating bats lives inside. We cannot leave them be.\" \n\n All the animals fell silent; they generally did not associate with bats. Only Dunn had visited that cave last spring, but he had long forgotten what it looked like inside. \n\n \"Let's go!\" Daly jumped onto the tips of the antlers. \"Even if you lose your way inside, my singing can lead us to the right path.\" \n\n They entered the cave just like that. The structure inside was intricate and complex, and it took Dunn and Daly quite some effort to find the injured bat family. Just as they were preparing to leave the cave, a gale blew outside, and countless snowflakes were carried by the wind, blocking all light. Dunn tried several more directions. More desperate than not finding the exit was the increasingly weak breathing of the bat family. \n\n Daly flew to his ear and began to sing. The golden melody guided and soothed Dunn's somewhat restless mood, and he walked along the direction where the notes lit up. Ten meters, fifty meters, one hundred meters... There was still no light from the cave entrance in sight. Daly realized that the price of reaching the exit might be higher than imagined. \n\n Without hesitation. \n\n She flew higher, to a place where Dunn couldn't see clearly, singing until there were few feathers left on her back, and she began to fall. \n\n There was still no light in sight.",
